  "_comment": "Model -> its list price, in the unit the model is billed in. A row with no \"unit\" is priced per 1,000,000 tokens: in (input/prompt), out (output/completion), cache_read (cached-input read), cache_write (cache-creation write). Otherwise \"unit\" is image (per_image, or tiers of {size: the largest WIDTHxHEIGHT it covers, quality, per_image} with the default_size and default_quality a call that names none is made at), second (per_second of video), minute (per_minute of audio) or character (per_mchar, per 1,000,000 characters). Every row names whose list price it is (vendor) and the day this table recorded it (recorded, YYYY-MM-DD). The builtin tier of personalclaw.routing.rates, which prices a call from it when the provider reports no cost and no rate the owner set, local engine or app declaration answers first. A model absent here is unpriced (honest: we never invent a price), a row prices its own model and that model's dated snapshots only, and no row prices a model free by its name: an open-weight model costs what the machine serving it bills. A token row's key is also in model_tokens.json. List prices change: the service that runs a model may bill differently, and a price set in Settings comes first.",
